    "cutouts": [
      "Fusion cut-out SVG: Cut-outs trace each connector’s visible outline, not the manufacturer’s recommended panel cut-out with clearance and tolerance.",
      "Rear panel view in the supplier drawing (V1.1) was drawn rotated 180° relative to how it actually mounts (text and port order appeared upside-down); all rear positions below were corrected for that rotation (real_x = width - raw_x, real_y = height - raw_y) before being entered, not read directly off the drawing's own pixel coordinates.",
      "Dimensions shown in red on the supplier drawing (12mm, 2.6mm, 6.1mm, 3.4mm, 11.5mm corner offsets; 240/110/30mm outline dims) are construction/outline guides only, per the drawing's own title block (丝印白色 vs 底托颜色 legend) — not treated as exact silkscreen-critical tolerances.",
      "The large rectangle with 'PureLink' wordmark + vents + 4 corner screws, and the two small vented end-cap views, are the enclosure's top view and side-profile views — mechanical/outline reference only, not a third silkscreen panel; not reproduced here.",
      "The separate bottom-face rectangle (Rating Label / MAC address / NOTES, 93.6mm callouts) is the function-coding legend face, not a front/rear silk panel; out of scope for this layout per the replicate-silkprint-panel skill (build via the Housing tab's own legend generator if needed, not as a panel).",
      "RJ45 'VCX' port on the rear shows an 'Amphenol' wordmark inside the jack outline in the supplier drawing — read as the connector manufacturer's own reference label on their CAD symbol, not as silkscreen text to reproduce, and omitted.",
      "HDMI (front INPUT, rear OUTPUT): locking-screw hole shown in the drawing directly above each HDMI jack — modelled as lock:true.",
      "USB-C (front INPUT 100W, rear DEVICE port 3): locking-screw hole shown directly above each — modelled as lock:true. Rear SERVICE USB-C shows no such hole — modelled as lock:false.",
      "EDID: 5-way DIP switch, count read directly off the drawing's own switch icon (5 toggle segments visible at high zoom).",
      "SW1/SW2 and RS-232 (LOCAL/PASS): each is one physical 2-row x 3-pin Phoenix terminal block (eb35x2) per the drawing's own icon shape, not two separate connectors.",
      "Positions measured from the supplier's silkprint drawing V1.1 (HDP-EUB40HCD-TX-DE0012, dated 2026-10-20) via pixel calibration against the drawing's own 240x30mm panel outline and 110mm depth side-view — not signed off."
    ],
    "silkscreen": [
      "Silkscreen SVG: Silk artwork replicated from the supplier's own silkprint drawing V1.1 (2026-10-20, HDP-EUB40HCD-TX-DE0012); dimensions on that drawing are guides only and were not treated as exact. Not compared against production silk files.",
      "Rear panel was drawn rotated 180° in the source file; corrected to true mounting orientation before replication (see cutout notes). titlePos:'top' on OUTPUT/DEVICE frames was re-derived from the corrected (un-rotated) pixel layout, not assumed from other library files.",
      "DANTE rear RJ45 carries the Audinate 'Dante' logo in the source drawing in place of a plain text label; represented here with func:'DANTE' (plain text), matching this repo's existing convention (see ipav-3x1-tranceiver-v0-2-layout.json) rather than attempting to reproduce the logo mark.",
